From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 07:07:46 -0500
Subject: feat: Open Link in Space (S-411)

A link's page menu has "Open Link in Space" ("Open link in Space" off the
Mac) after Open Link in Split View, in a window with more than one Space:
a row for each other Space, in switcher order, a Space with an independent
session marked as Move to Space marks it. A row opens the link in a new tab
filed in that Space and made in its jar, so its first request carries that
Space's cookies, and the window goes to that Space. The Space named wins
over a route (spaces::ScopedNewTabSpace, read by ChooseSpaceForNewTab). Not
in a popup, an app, a private window or a peek over the page (menus M14,
spaces B46).

Why: GitHub issue 75, as Zen has it; the owner asked for the issues'
improvements on 2026-11-04.
Removable when: never as a feature.
